Z||000026||LarryB||09-06-2001||06:45 PM||||It's because people will jokingly (at least usually jokingly) make reference or infer that they share other traits besides physical appearance, even if no harm is intended by the original poster. It's too easy for this kind of stuff to get out of control. <P>And, whether it's right or wrong, a woman who poses in the nude for a photographer and allows them to be made public isn't usually considered to be of, how shall I put it, very high moral character. <P>Would you think it funny if someone posted your first name and phone # in a gay bar or on alt.motss on Usenet or took out an ad in some underground newspaper and you started getting phone calls and emails from gay guys trolling for "good times" in Toronto, even if it were done as a joke?  I sure wouldn't. <P>||||reg||13
Z||000027||Mach10||09-06-2001||06:49 PM||||I hate to bore it into your thick skull, but it IS sexual harrassment. The fact that if someone had substituted my photo for Jens there wouldn't be an uproar is immaterial. It was a tasteless remark with sexual conntations. Deal with it.<P>It would be the same thing if someone took a pornographic picture and welded a photo of Jens head to it. Whether or not it causes an uproar is a moot point. If you make a racist comment in a thread, and no-one comments, is the mark any less vile? Extreme? I don't think so. Sexism is a form of racism. Sexual harrassment is a form of sexism.<P>I won't argue that the comment was made malisciously. It probably wasn't. Hell, I let slip offensive things all the time. I won't dwell on the comment, as I'm sure that Jen won't. If whoever had made the comment (can't remember login, too lazy to look up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )has appologized, then this particular issue is closed. I think that Jen takes more issue to the fact (correct me if I'm wrong, please) that some people here don't seem to understand that the comment was both hurtful and sexist.<BR>Try and look at it from her point of view, alright JohnnyK?||||reg||13
Z||000028||LZeitgeist||09-06-2001||07:42 PM||||Jennifer - <P>Since you *were* offended by the pic and comments in question, I apologize. <P>However, (asked very gently) how are any of us to know that you are offended until you let us know? I have quite a few female friends who would have thought the comparision between a nude model and them to be funny... I'm not guessing what their reaction would be, I *know* what their reaction would be, because I know them well. <P>Thank you for letting us know what your thoughts are, and since you were offended, I apologize for the comment I added to the mix - I will happly go edit my comment back out of the other thread to prevent you further embarassment. <P><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001||||reg||1
