Z||000036||Fierochic88||09-06-2001||09:26 PM||||Guys, Guys, Guys (and the women who responded too)-<P>I'm not knocking anybody for posting pics of nude women.  I have many guy friends and I certainly appreciate male humor, just not at my expense.  You guys can look at whatever you want and enjoy it by all means!  While I realize this was all meant in good fun, and I am not extremely mad about it, I began this topic to request that that "fun" be ended before it gets taken to an even worse level, which, unfortunately seems to happen on here sometimes.  <P>My apologies to those who can't see where I'm coming from, but maybe if we drag you around a little, you might develop a better understanding.<P>And as far as upsetting my dad?  Well to tell you the truth, I doubt he has even seen this crap.  My whole point, and Joe's, was that he could possibly come across it, and while I'm not "12", I am only a few years into being "a grown up woman" and I am very close to my dad, and I know a lot of dad's are very protective of their daughters, regardless of how old they are.  <P>My point was that before people make comments they should think about how other people may possibly recieve them, not that everything you say will make every one happy all the time, just try and use a little bit of empathy if possible.<P>Jennifer||||reg||1
Z||000037||Fierochic88||09-06-2001||09:31 PM||||BTW - I do have a sense of humor...<P>If I were that chick I would have at least picked a fiero that had all the same color body panels!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  At least it had a 3.4 in it.<P>Jennifer<P>I wasn't offended by the pic itself, just the fact that people chose to involve me in it.||||reg||1
Z||000038||firstfiero||09-06-2001||09:32 PM||||    I agree completly... and now knowing how you feel it would be very wrong of anyone to do something like that again at your expense. I'm glad you saw it as a joke though and not as someone trying to be mean.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000039||Mach10||09-06-2001||09:44 PM||||Ok, now the order's all messed up. FirstFiero and I were having an entertaining little spat on the OTHER post... Here's my latest contribution, and my new rebuttal:<P>quote:<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>By FirstFiero:<BR>Their is harrasment where out in the world would only come into play if I continued after she told me to beat it. <P>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<P><BR>Fair enough. <BR>Now ask yourself this: This is a family forum, Cliff would like to keep it that way. Is sexual harrassment a Good Thing to have on a family forum? Would you rather trumpet on about freedom of speech, or would you like to respect the fact that the comment was offensive to the party, and back off? How is your right to "free speech" more important than the feelings of another member who has done nothing (that I know of) to you? Just because it debases only one individual, does it make it any better than using a term like ni&&er, or ch1nk, or sp1nk? (Sorry cliff, I modified the terms so that the spyders wouldn't catch them. No reason to defame your sight while excersizing a socio-political debate)<BR>I am truly sick of you self-righteous assholes who bleat on about freedom of speech. You taint the whole purpose for which the idea was born. Freedom of speech was created so that YOU could live your life how you wanted it, so that you wouldn't have to feel the burdon of oppression over your shoulders. Instead, you take it at face value, and consider it your god-given right to trample all over other people on the basis that you can say what you like. Know what? Racism and sexism are both forms of oppression, and are VERY rampant in your beloved United States. Free society indeed.<BR>Go ahead, ramble on about how you are allowed to say such things. But maybe, JUST MAYBE, consider that while you MAY say such things, you might consider excersizing your right not to say it, and lift some burden off another's shoulders.<P><BR>===&gt; Place First Fiero's prev. comment here:<P>My argument isn't really that Sexual harrassment as a matter for the Justice department (although it should be), but rather that it's still wrong. She was offended, as she posted here, and many members were good enough to erase their comments. That's cool. The fact remains though, that the comment was directed AT a person specifically, and could easily have been construed as sexually harrassing. This is as bad as racism.<P>===&gt; Place FirstFiero's latest comment here...<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>By First Fiero<B><BR>I agree completly... and now knowing how you feel it would be very wrong of anyone to do something like that again at your expense. I'm glad you saw it as a joke though and not as someone trying to be mean.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm glad you said that. I withdraw my previous rude comments. The arguments still stand, if anyone wants to debate them, but FirstFiero has shown to me that he can be a considerate person if he wants to be    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000040||JohnnyK||09-06-2001||10:35 PM||||Drop the sexual harrassment.. It WASN'T sexual harassment. See, monkeyman telling me to go away could be harassment. I understand that you guys all have to insult me to stand up for the women of this forum and look like heros, and I'm sure they do too, so don't worry about it. I'm not insulting anyone. I'm just saying, it wasn't even bad.<P>Veronica: Umm, I do work? But I don't know anyone who's work gave them sexual harassment lessons.<P>ps: I was trying to find a picture of a naked man that sort of looks like me and post my picture beside it, but didn't look for too long. See, if you manipulate it and put my face on a guy, that is TOTALLY different then what happened here.<P>edited to add: Btw, have some of you not even lOOKED at the thread and just started jumping in for the hell of it? No one manipulated any picture. All they did was MENTION a resemblence in about 2 responses.<p>[This message has been edited by JohnnyK (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000041||JSocha||09-06-2001||10:36 PM||||<B>What is sexual harassment?</B><P>Sexual harassment is any kind of sexual behavior that is unwelcome and/or inappropriate for the work place. Sexual harassment can embrace verbal harassment(i.e. derogatory comments or dirty jokes under the right circumstances), visual harassment (i.e. derogatory or embarrassing posters, cartoons, drawing, etc.), physical harassment, and sexual favors (i.e. sexual advances, confrontation with sexual demands.)<P>Sexual harassment is defined as "unwelcomed sexual advances or conduct". Sexual harassment also includes animosity that is gender-based and a sexually charged work environment. In the work place, sexual harassment can come from the owner, supervisor, manager, lead person, foreperson, co-worker and/or customer.<P><I>However, sexual harassment does not restrict itself to the work place. Sexual harassment can come in many forms. For example, sexual harassment can also be found in schools.</I><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000042||JohnnyK||09-07-2001||02:04 AM||||Stimpy: Anyways.. I'm not trying to win anything (notice how i haven't actually really argued and specific point). I just spouted off my views, which, obviously, were not those of the majority.||||reg||1
Z||000043||Urchin||09-07-2001||02:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>[b]What is sexual harassment?</B><P>Sexual harassment is any kind of sexual behavior that is unwelcome and/or inappropriate for the work place. Sexual harassment can embrace verbal harassment(i.e. derogatory comments or dirty jokes under the right circumstances), visual harassment (i.e. derogatory or embarrassing posters, cartoons, drawing, etc.), physical harassment, and sexual favors (i.e. sexual advances, confrontation with sexual demands.)<P>Sexual harassment is defined as "unwelcomed sexual advances or conduct". Sexual harassment also includes animosity that is gender-based and a sexually charged work environment. In the work place, sexual harassment can come from the owner, supervisor, manager, lead person, foreperson, co-worker and/or customer.<P><I>However, sexual harassment does not restrict itself to the work place. Sexual harassment can come in many forms. For example, sexual harassment can also be found in schools.</I><P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I don't think you can argue with that Johnny.  In all fairness, I didn't find the topic at hand to be overly offensive either.  But as I said before... what you or I think is irrelevant.  The post did not effect you or I, it was in reference to Fierochic, and that makes your opinion nothing more than just that... an opinion.  If she was offended by the posts then she is fully within her rights to dispute it.  However, I don't think this is even about that anymore.  It seems to me that the reason why you are taking a lot of flack from other members is for your lack of respect in certain comments you have made.  From what I have seen, you have been relatively rude in certain posts, and that is the problem, ...how you presented your thoughts.  What was it you said earlier?  ..."Suck it up" <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">  <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000044||Mach10||09-07-2001||02:10 AM||||Johnny: Go stand in the corner.<BR>Jsocha: *applause*<BR>Urchin: *applause*<P><BR>I vote that we all just drop this, and let all of this nastiness fade into obscurity. Bygones be bygones (whatever the hell they are...) etc.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000045||Monkeyman||09-07-2001||06:09 AM||||JohnnyK--I wasn't trying to harrass you by telling you to go away.  I was simply stating my feelings.  You should consider going away for a while until you grow up some.  This is not a cut, either.  There is another PFF member that used to cause some trouble, went away, apparently grew up some and returned.  Although I haven't read all of his posts since he returned, from what I've read it seems that he's a much nicer forum member now.  Follow his lead.<P>The last thing I need to do here is try to impress any of the forum members, either male or female.  Honestly, I couldn't care less if they think I'm a hero or a jerk.  I don't know Fierochic so there's no reason for me to impress her.  I like to feel that I'm impressing my wife and my son, but that's about it.  (And, yes.  I did read the other thread before I posted here.)<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000046||EdsB52||09-07-2001||06:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>[b]What is sexual harassment?</B><P>Sexual harassment is any kind of sexual behavior that is unwelcome and/or inappropriate for the work place. Sexual harassment can embrace verbal harassment(i.e. derogatory comments or dirty jokes under the right circumstances), visual harassment (i.e. derogatory or embarrassing posters, cartoons, drawing, etc.), physical harassment, and sexual favors (i.e. sexual advances, confrontation with sexual demands.)<P>Sexual harassment is defined as "unwelcomed sexual advances or conduct". Sexual harassment also includes animosity that is gender-based and a sexually charged work environment. In the work place, sexual harassment can come from the owner, supervisor, manager, lead person, foreperson, co-worker and/or customer.<P><I>However, sexual harassment does not restrict itself to the work place. Sexual harassment can come in many forms. For example, sexual harassment can also be found in schools.</I><P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Sexual harassment is any kind of sexual behavior that is unwelcome and/or inappropriate for the work place."<P>This is not a workplace!<P>"Sexual harassment also includes animosity that is gender-based and a sexually charged work environment."<P>I said, this is not a workplace! Good definition Jeff. Generally, harassment of a sexual nature that is outside of the workplace is considered an assualt, but is almost never actioned these days, and if it is, it's actioned civilly. But the operative word is "unwelcome." Jennifer carries herself in here in such a manner that she does not welcome or warrant that kind of treatment. I cannot say that for all female members. I wish everyone would lay off Johnny. After all, he didn't paste the pics together (per my understanding), he just remarked about it. ||||reg||1
Z||000047||JSocha||09-07-2001||08:47 AM||||The above statement came off of a photocopy we were handed out from a book called "Avoiding Sexual Harrassment in the Workplace".<P>However, if I time and can get ahold of it today from the Production Manager, they give many more examples of where "Sexual Harrassment" is found other then the workplace...and yes...outside the workplace it is also called assault.<P>However, go into a supermarket, bar and/or restraunt and play touchy-feely with a women (man might like it) and she will charge you with assault and sexual harrassment.<P>My wife finally filed charges two years ago against a guy here in town that would "goose" her and grab at her...well...her chest...and make unwarranted advances and statements to her everytime he saw her in a store or on the street.  He did it to quite a few women, not just my wife.<P>But my wife, she made the complainte and it was filled out under both "assault/battery" and "sexual harrassment", we went to court and he was charged under both and was gone for a little under a year.<P>When he got out, he left Rugby.<P>EDIT (Added):  Was Assault & "Battery" along with "Sexual Harrassment".<p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000048||87GTZ34||09-07-2001||10:09 AM||||Jen, It's unfortunate that you got mixed up in this 'humorous' post by someone's lack of thought for you or your family.  I am in agreement that while attempts at humor & entertainment are quite allright, people should consider the impact of thier actions when directed at individiduals (also groups but most definately individuals) especially in a community of which they are both a part of (cyber neighbors by interests and associations).  But as I've grown from your age to mine (I've got almost 20 on you), I've come to the realization that my perception of normal people's thoughts, words and actions are different than mine (for the worse).  When I was younger, I thought that 10 - 20 percent of the population were jerks, (stonger words used in my mind) and lacked the ability to think rationally before directing their energy to actions and words.  Today that is reversed, I believe that only about 10 percent of the population take the 1 second to think, make a judgement and be considerate of others before acting.  So I applaud you for urging others to think first but I won't hold my breath.  Hopefully, Cliff's forum and its members will prove me wrong for your sake and others in the future that will be offended by someone elses mis-directed attempts at entertaining.  <BR>Note to others - my negative comment on human behavior is not directed at anyone or any group in particular.  I think both of these posts escalated quite a bit from where they started and emotion changed main points of everyone's posts except FieroChic88s.<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000049||LZeitgeist||09-07-2001||10:52 AM||||It's a shame this whole situation came to all this, because it could have *all* been avoided by a couple *very simple* things happening...<P>1) Jen's boyfriend or Dad letting her know about the thread.<P>2) Jen posting *two simple words*: "I'm offended."<P><BR>Had these two simple things happened, I feel *quite* sure that the entire original thread would have stopped, and edits and apologies would have begun rolling in IMMEDIATELY. There was no need for an entire second thread.<P>As you can see from the apologies, Jen, boyfriend and Dad, NO INSULT WAS INTENDED. Possible poor taste? Granted, yes, according to some peoples' sensibilities. The Internet is a big place, though - in it reside infinite numbers of variences in senses of humor. However, my other opinion stands... if Jen had *not* been offended, I feel it would have been O.K. - if Jen had found it humorous in any way, I rather doubt that your "stunned silence"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> would have continued.<P>Just my two cents, hopefully the last I will offer on the subject since I'd like to see this whole thing die down so that we may all go on to more enjoyable subjects, and so Jen may avoid continued embarassment from our ill-made choices in the matter.||||reg||1
Z||000050||Jaygee79||09-07-2001||01:53 PM||||Jen, I"m sorry all of this happened.<P>JohnnyK, do you realize just how much of a jerk you make yourself out to be on here?  Who cares if you're not offended by it?  It has nothing to do with you.  Just because you found it funny and unoffensive doesn't mean everyone else has to feel the same way.  Grow up.||||reg||1
Z||000051||Butter||09-07-2001||02:30 PM||||Something I heard a long time ago. It went something like;<P>"Remember to engage your brain before you start your mouth."<P>also the other one I like;<P>"A little respect goes a long way."<P>Sometimes I may slip a little on some of that so yall all help keep in the middle of the road. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000052||JohnnyK||09-07-2001||04:12 PM||||Mach10: If you want this to fade away into obscurity, don't try to fuel the fire by saying such things as "Go stand in the corner"<P>Monkeyman: I'm not intending to be rude, I'm just stating my opinion that things could be a lot worse.  In my short (long?) 20 years on this earth, I have learned one thing that I swear by every day now, and it took me about 19.5 years to learn.. "****  happens. Suck it up" I'm not insulting or trying to be a jerk at all.. <P>Anyways, I'm sorry you all took this the wrong way, but I wish you people WOULD realise that no one would have made a big deal out of this had this been a man... Anyways, feel free to take a picture of a naked man and stick my picture BESIDE it...||||reg||5
Z||000053||RobertVol||09-07-2001||05:17 PM||||Well I have to say everytime I go away on business and then come back to the Forum I finds a neat little OVERBLOWN topic. This is a prime example.....<P>There are many points to this ... lets break them down:<P>1. Jennifer was offended. (point understood)<P>2. JohnnyK felt it was not that big of a deal. To be honest,I agree with him. I mean in the time it took to type how offended someone is you could accidently click on alot of offensive sites. The world is not coming to end. Hit the wrong number on the remote and your watching tits on "Skin a MaX" instead of ESPN. What are we going to do? write a post  with 100 reponses about that? And to the comments made about the post,,,, Well..I have to say I have been around too long and through too much to think this is that big of a deal. Because Johnny voiced his opinion and its not the popular one, so what! <P>He stated his true thoughts. I know I will get killed for this, and I am not siding with JohnnyK, and it may be the posting was horrible, but I have seen alot of things worse posted here that were alot more offensive than that. You can post my name next to any fricking picture you want. That is juvenile. There are some on my Web site. Put mine next to a 350 lb hog in a bathing suit.  I could care less. It does not change fact that once Jennifer stated she was offended..Johnny made a comment that you may not agree with but hey!!!!!, <BR>Jennifer is a big girl, she may not need or want all this hoopla on this crap in this post. Anyone think of that? Johnny made a comment. Let Jennifer e mail him or tell him she did not like his comment. She may,(Believe it or not) be able to defend herself. <P>3. JohnnyK seems to be upset because everytime anything is said about a woman, all the the little so called "Men" come to the defense of the women and start posting like mad. Trying to impress someone or something. With that said, I understand what johnnyK is saying. It happens all the time. I am kinda of disgusted at the sucking up to. BUT That is not to say that all the men who have sided on this are doing it for that reason. I know that is not the case for people posting on this like Stimpy and Monkeyman and I have seen many posts from older males who probably have children and may find certain things wrong with it. I understand your concern, but COME ON GUYS!!, you have got to see that what Johnny is saying is somewhat true. I would bet half if not more of the longest posts on the forum are about women being hurt or being flirted with.. Shall we do a history to prove this?<P>Its a sad fact that alot of guys in here, would love to stand up here, because they dont have the guts to do it in person. Its easy to hide behind a keyoard and be Mr. Tough Guy and stand up for women.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Again this is  not a slight on the men who REALLY feel this was inappropriate.  If you TRULY feel that way, you are entitled to that feeling. But the ones in here who are not ( and you know who you are), get a life... So I do believe Jennifer has a point and is valid but for everyone to jump on Johnny well I find it a little "out of line"<P>All this to say:<P>Jennifer - I never saw the posting, but if you were offended, I am sorry<P>Johnny - I agree, it wasnt that big of a deal. but if she is offended. Apologize and be done with it. <P>Well since this just board on the Web and not REAL life, screw the flame suit! flame all ya want. I could care less.<P>This stuff is getting way out of control<P><BR>BTW..Fiero Fans - Anyone got a 88gt t top they want to give away?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <P>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 09-07-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000054||DRH||09-07-2001||05:56 PM||||Robert,<P>I think you missed the point:<P>Jennifer started this post as an explanation of how she felt about the other post. She didn't demand anything... just explained her point of view.<P>The original poster from the other thread apologized.<P>Then JohnnyK posts:<BR>"Oh JESUS! SUCK IT UP! Someone posted a picture of you as a JOKE because it sort of resembled you. boohoo"<P>What <B>possible</B> intent could this have had other than to start some sh!t? The whole 'taking up for a woman' argument is his usual attempt to divert blame to anybody but himself. Just like the 'Cliff must be having a bad day' comment. It's NEVER JohnnyK's fault.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> You bought that???<P>||||reg||1
Z||000055||JohnnyK||09-07-2001||08:58 PM||||Oh man, give it up. I wasn't trying to start anything. I just stated my thoughts, and me saying you guys suck up to women is not to divert the blame.. If you'd realize, a LOT of people have said that in the past. "Nothings Johnny's fault". Cliff obviously got upset, I tried to add some humour, obviously it didn't work. No one is trying to divert the blame of anything (mostly because there is nothing to put blame on), well, except for you and a few others trying to put it on me. Oh well. I agree, my above comment was a little harsh, and if i could go back and reword it into something a little less dramatic, I would. (editing is not going back in time).<P>RObertvol: Nope, but I have an 85 SE you can take for almost nothing (lets say, 650 american..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by JohnnyK (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000056||DRH||09-07-2001||09:38 PM||||JohnnyK,<P>How could you NOT see where such a harsh statement would lead?<P>She posted her opinion on the subject. You in affect said her opinion was wrong and she was a crybaby. You didn't even present an argument to support your opinion. You just flamed her.<P>Later in the thread you keep mentioning how differently YOU would feel about a similar situation involving you. I think we all understand it wouldn't bother you. I find that a bit suspect though since you haven't managed to find a pic of yourself to put up here yet. Don't worry about finding the naked guy, I'm sure a lot of members on here can help you out if you just post yours.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>You don't have to share her views, you don't even have to agree with them, it would make you seem a lot less of a jerk if you showed some indication that you at least understood them though.<P>||||reg||1
